// A perfectly ordinary permit that was reported VACUOUS -- a working rule declared dead, and the
// advice that follows a VACUOUS verdict is to delete it.
//
// A field's domain is the literals the policy names plus values it does not name, so that both
// matching and not-matching stay reachable. For a long time the only extra value was ABOVE the
// largest literal, which makes `==` and `>` satisfiable and leaves `<` and `<=` with no witness
// at all: the domain for the field below was {25000, 25001}, and neither is less than 25000.
//
// It survived because every fixture that would have caught it compared for EQUALITY. The article
// this came from writes `context.input.cost < 25000` in its human-approval policy, which is how
// it was found.
permit (
    principal,
    action == AgentCore::Action::"execute_trade",
    resource
)
when {
    context.input.cost < 25000
};
